    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="21.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 21.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="508–509" ed="#liebermann"/>En Westsexenelahge ne vocherad il mie sun guarant, devant iceo qu'il seit mis en guage.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="508–509" ed="#liebermann"/>E<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.c"/> en Westsexenelae ne vocherad mie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.20"/> soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.4"/> seignour<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.d"/> warant, . . . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.b"/> iceo que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.17"/> seit mis en guage.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="508–509" ed="#liebermann"/>Nemo autem cogetur warantum uocare, antequam calumpniator producat en gaige manu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.d-2"/> sexta.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="21.3" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="264" ed="#robertson"/>En Westsexenelahge ne vocherad il mie sun guarant devant iceo qu'il seit mis en guage.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="508–509" ed="#liebermann"/>21, 3. Im Westsachsen-Rechtsgebiet aber braucht er auf seinen Gewährsmann nicht früher sich zu berufen, als bis [Kläg]er in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_21-3.lnote.de1.c"/> Pfandleistung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_21-3.lnote.de.1"/> versetzt ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">21, 3. In the West Saxon legal district, however, he need not appeal to his warrantor before the [plaint]iff has been put to the giving of pledge.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="265" ed="#robertson"/>In the province of Wessex he shall not call upon his warrantor until the claimant has put himself under pledge.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 264–265 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 508–509, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze aus HkL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply from HkL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">E en W. <hi rend="italic">ziehen irrig zu</hi> 21,2 <hi rend="italic">L und I's Edd.: aber einen Gegensatz zu</hi> 21,2 <hi rend="italic">fordert diese nachträgliche Ausnahme eines Localrechts</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">E en W. is wrongly attached to 21,2 by L and I’s Edd.: but this subsequent exception for a local law requires a contrast with 21,2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nor <hi rend="italic">Io; streiche als aus voriger Zeile wiederholt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nor Io; delete as repeated from the preceding line</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">une <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">une Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-3.lnote.oe.d-2" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">509</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">aus</hi> 21, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from 21, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_21-3.lnote.de1.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">509</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Pfand giebt für Klagedurchführung und Busse, falls er sachfällig wird</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">gives a pledge for carrying through the suit and for compensation, should he lose the case</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_21-3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 21{2}. 21, 1{4}</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 21{2}. 21, 1{4}</seg></note>
      </div>
